            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0905" n="835" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg835"/>

                <head>No. 537.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Wallace.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 28,
                        1883</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 56.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your No. 169, of the 25th ultimo, has been
                    received. It presents a new regulation by the Sublime Porte for the storage of
                    petroleum, and gives copy of your protest of January 20 last, to the minister
                    for foreign affairs, respecting the subject.</p>
                <p>In approving your course and awaiting further developments with interest, I can
                    do no less than say that the Department commends your energetic and timely
                    action.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
